  "raw_text": "Step 1: The given parametric equations for the line are:\n\\[x = 8 + 2t\\]\n\\[y = -1 + 3t\\]\n\nStep 2: To express the line in the form \\(y = mx + b\\), we need to eliminate the parameter \\(t\\).\n\nStep 3: From the first equation, solve for \\(t\\):\n\\[t = \\frac{x - 8}{2}\\]\n\nStep 4: Substitute this expression for \\(t\\) into the second equation:\n\\[y = -1 + 3\\left(\\frac{x - 8}{2}\\right)\\]\n\nStep 5: Simplify the equation:\n\\[y = -1 + \\frac{3(x - 8)}{2}\\]\n\\[y = -1 + \\frac{3x - 24}{2}\\]\n\\[y = -1 + \\frac{3x}{2} - 12\\]\n\\[y = \\frac{3x}{2} - 13\\]\n\nStep 6: The equation is now in the form \\(y = mx + b\\), where \\(m = \\frac{3}{2}\\) and \\(b = -13\\).\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, -13\\right)}<|im_end|>",
